    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick breakdown of the stages in a standard CI/CD pipeline? specifically looking for code commit, testing, staging, and prod deployment. also need to know what kind of gates we should have at each step to make sure nothing breaks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard CI/CD pipeline commonly flows from **Code Commit** to **Testing**, then to **Staging**, and finally to **Production Deployment**. At the commit stage, automated linting and unit tests act as essential quality gates. During testing, integration and end-to-end tests confirm functionality, while staging gates involve user acceptance testing (UAT) and performance checks. Finally, before production, security scans and manual sign-offs serve as crucial gates to ensure a stable and secure release.",
      "source": "target",
